WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Members of Parliament,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.000
My political advisers have advised me to keep this meeting.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000
They advised me to speak to you from this place about the climate crisis.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
They advised me to take the word climate crisis into my mouth.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
It would be better to speak about climate opportunities or climate challenges.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
That sounds more enthusiastic and excited, more like you know me.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
But I'm not telling the honest story with that.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
And I'm not telling that because I know you're going to quit.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
It's very simple.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
If I say we have to be able to keep barbecuing, I rise in the polls.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
If I say I'm going to introduce a meat tax, I won't be chosen.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.360
But you deserve the honest story.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:00.440
The honest story is that the earth is warming up dangerously quickly.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.160
The honest story is that corona was a crisis of a clueless size...

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.400
...compared to what is still to be seen due to climate change.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.080
The honest story is that you only need to remember one figure of this statement.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.720
The figure that made me see that poldering over solutions is not enough.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.720
Five metres.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:30.720
If everything is against it, the world's sea level has risen by almost five metres in 2150.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.720
This is not something that happens overnight.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:41.720
By the end of this century, the water for the Dutch coast could be two or three metres higher.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.720
Sooner or later, we will have to give a price to the sea for parts of our country.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:54.280
The children who are born now would have to say goodbye to the west of the Netherlands.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:00.720
Their children could still experience that almost the entire Netherlands becomes uninhabitable.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:09.840
The probable sea level rise is lower, but a responsible government cannot escape the most optimistic scenarios.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.480
Five meters. The survival of the Netherlands is at stake.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:22.720
In the cabinet I have been able to lead so far, I have given the climate insufficient attention.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.240
And I'm sorry about that.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.680
To all of you, I say, the cabinet is determined to take the lost time.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.960
That is why a legislation package is going to the House of Representatives today...

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:41.640
that forms the basis for a fast and intensive transition towards sustainability.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.240
The message is clear.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.480
The free will is over.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.600
No more silly little things.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.200
The most important points of departure from the plan.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:58.360
1. What is polluting will become more expensive and eventually forbidden.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.880
This will limit the waste of raw materials and energy.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.840
2. We do this together.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.840
The pain of the transition is shared as honestly as possible.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.240
The strongest shoulders carry the heaviest burdens.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.840
and no one can remain in poverty of energy.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.040
3. The government finances the transition with loans for the future.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.440
We can pay for this.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:30.240
4. The Dutch business world is made future-proof with generous government support.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.840
Whoever puts the hack in the sand, must close the doors.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.920
This also applies to companies in the industry and agriculture.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:44.160
And finally, number five. We let go of the pursuit of endless economic growth.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.520
If the economy grows during the transition, that's fine.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.280
If it shrinks, we can handle it.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.720
Our plan is comprehensive.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.480
Yes, it will sometimes hurt and lead to frustrations, I understand that very well.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.840
But it only works if we can do it in its entirety.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.480
We cannot tackle the industry if we ignore the landlord.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.440
It makes no sense to reduce the feed stack if wealthy consumers

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.720
then keep buying just as much meat, but from another country.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.720
And we don't have to do this alone.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.480
We can draw on our European allies,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.120
who are already a step further in the transition to clean energy,

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.800
a plant-based diet and the reuse of raw materials.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:35.760
Our economy will become more sustainable, more just and more independent.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.720
The effort of this incredibly large operation is freedom.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:46.000
And if I'm not talking about the freedom to fly to Barcelona for a ten,

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:52.440
then I'm talking about the freedom to breathe without getting harmful substances in your lungs.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.200
The freedom not to be threatened by heat waves, floods and droughts.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.200
The freedom not to have to worry about your future.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.560
This freedom is now being threatened.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:12.120
And sometimes there comes a moment that we have to protect our freedom and show what it is worth to us.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:18.160
Sometimes there comes a moment that the interests of a species go beyond that of the individual.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.080
This is such a moment.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.160
We choose to tackle the climate crisis now.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.760
We have the means, the opportunities and the manpower to do this.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:36.920
We are getting better at it, the world is getting better at it, and the future is getting better at it.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.560
So let's hope that this statement will soon come true.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.080
Because this wasn't real. I'm not Mark Rutte.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.560
But imagine, I say these words, just like I'm doing it now.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:56.000
You listen to it, the politicians listen to it, Mark listens to it and thinks, hey damn, what a great guy who's in there.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.080
I was just a bit more like him.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.120
And before he knows it, because that's how it is when people tell each other stories...

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.320
he starts talking like me.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.800
Thinking like me.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.880
Acting like me.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.840
And starts talking like you.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.400
And thinking and acting.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:19.600
And no one can imagine that it ever was different.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.600
Thank you.
